    "content": "\"Buffalo\" most commonly refers to the American bison (Bison bison), a large, hump-backed, shaggy-maned bovid native to North America, often erroneously called buffalo. True buffaloes are African buffalo or Asian water buffalo, which belong to different genera. They are herbivores and key cultural symbols.Key Facts About American Bison (\"Buffalo\")Appearance: Shaggy brown coat, large shoulder hump, and short, curved horns, weighing up to 2,000 pounds.Habitat & Range: Once ranged from Alaska to Mexico; today, they live in highly fragmented herds in national parks, wildlife refuges, and private ranches in the U.S. and Canada.Diet: Herbivores feeding on grasses, weeds, and leafy plants.Conservation Status: While once near extinction, conservation efforts have established numerous herds.Key Facts About True BuffaloesAfrican Buffalo (Syncerus caffer): Known for being unpredictable and dangerous, they are found in Sub-Saharan Africa and have a near-threatened conservation status.Water Buffalo (Bubalus bubalis): Primarily domesticated in Asia for labor and dairy, they are highly endangered in the wild.Differences: Bison vs. BuffaloHorns: Bison have shorter, sharper, black horns designed for fighting, while African buffalo have larger, curved horns that form a \"boss\" or shield.Appearance: Bison have a prominent shoulder hump; buffalo do not.\"Buffalo\" in CultureNational Mammal: The American bison is the national mammal of the United States.Cultural Significance: Known as tatanka in Lakota, they were vital for food, clothing, and shelter for many Indigenous peoples.Buffalo - WikipediaBubalina, a subtribe of the tribe Bovini within the subfamily Bovinae. African buffalo or Cape buffalo (Syncerus caffer) Bubalus, ...WikipediaBUFFALO Definition & Meaning - Merriam-WebsterApr 18, 2026 — Kids Definition * : any of several wild mammals related to oxen: as. * a. : water buffalo. * b. : cape buffalo. * c. : a large sha...Merriam-WebsterBison vs Buffalo: Scientif